<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Tyus Jones on $3.88m in 2026-27?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Jones is paid <strong>$3.88m</strong> because he is a backup point guard in his thirties, and the veteran minimum is what that job pays now.</p>
<ul>
<li>He has one of the best assist to turnover ratios in league history, which is the skill clubs keep signing him for.</li>
<li>He is listed at 6’0″, and his defense is the reason he has never held a starting job for long.</li>
<li>He was paid <strong>$15m</strong> at <a href="/teams/memphis-grizzlies/">Memphis</a> in 2022-23 and has not been near that figure since.</li>
<li>Veteran minimum contracts are partly reimbursed by the league, so they cost a club less than the listed number.</li>
<li>He turned 30 in May, which is the age at which backup guards stop getting multi-year offers.</li>
</ul>
<p>He and <a href="/players/demar-derozan/">DeMar DeRozan</a> are paid exactly the same figure this season.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
